 35S  c  2026Jo01: A 66-MeV dispersion-matched proton beam was produced from the
 35S 2c  Separated Sector Cyclotron facility of iThemba LABS, South Africa. The 
 35S 3c  target was 1-mg/cm{+2}, 99.24%-enriched {+36}S powder encapsulated     
 35S 4c  between two 0.5-|mm Mylar foils. The outgoing deuteron and triton      
 35S 5c  reaction products momentum-analyzed by the K600                        
 35S 6c  quadrupole-dipole-dipole magnetic spectrometer and detected by the     
 35S 7c  focal-plane detector consisting of two multiwire drift chambers (MWDC) 
 35S 8c  and a plastic scintillator downstream. Measured |s(E{-d},|q). Deduced  
 35S 9c  98 levels, single-neutron spectroscopic factors and strengths from     
 35S Ac  adiabatic distorted-wave approximation (ADWA) calculations using the   
 35S Bc  zero-range code DWUCK4.                                                
